# React Three Fiber & 3D

Apply when editing files under `src/components/backgrounds/three/`:

## Performance

- Never allocate inside `useFrame` (`new THREE.Vector3()`, etc.) — use `useMemo`/`useRef`.
- Prefer `InstancedMesh` for many identical geometries.
- Mutate refs/uniforms per frame — do not drive continuous animation via React state.

## Stack

- Use `@react-three/drei` helpers and `useFrame` — never raw `requestAnimationFrame`.
- Sync with UI via `AnimationOrchestrator` / `useOrchestrator()` from `src/lib/`.

## Typing

- Type refs: `useRef<THREE.Mesh>(null)`.
- Cast materials: `mesh.material as THREE.ShaderMaterial` before uniform access.
- Named prop interfaces — no `any[]`; no `@ts-nocheck`.

Load `.cursor/skills/frontend/threejs/SKILL.md` for shader, cleanup, and audio patterns.
